            "I know this pain very well. In my second UPSC Prelims, on 5 June 2022, I cleared CSAT, but General Studies stayed just out of reach. Before that, I had missed the M.Sc. cut-off at Delhi University with 79%, the cut-off sitting just above it. Being so close is a special kind of hurt. If I had failed by a lot, I could have said, “I wasn't ready.” Missing by a little leaves you with a hundred “if onlys”.",
