            "One story that helped me a lot is in Wings of Fire, Dr A. P. J. Abdul Kalam's autobiography. As a young man, his dream was to be an Air Force pilot. He came ninth in the selection, and there were only eight places. He missed his dream by one place. He writes about how broken he felt, and how he went to Rishikesh and met a teacher there who helped him accept it and look for his own path. That one place he missed led him, eventually, to the work for which India remembers him.",
