            "Viktor Frankl's Man's Search for Meaning helped with a deeper question: why am I doing this at all? When I looked honestly, I found that I had wanted the IAS partly to prove I was special. Slowly, studying ethics, society and history, that changed. My “why” became serving people and sharing knowledge. And I realised that the “why” can be met by more than one road. The exam is one road. It's not the only one.",
